equest preserves the evidence and requires approval before any annotation correction or changed performance evaluation.\n\nThe practical F2 operating point yields approximately 29.2 true failures per 100 issued flags and misses 38.9 per 100 annotated failures, with 18.75 false flags per 100 successful segments. This trade-off comes from fold-specific training-selected thresholds. It neither establishes a universal cutoff nor supports false alarms/hour or prospective early warning.\n\nThe64-case blinded human-review package is prepared, but no ratings have been received or supplied by the agent. Annotation/boundary validation therefore remains pending. Eventual agreement must report cannot-determine responses and explicit denominators, and cannot be interpreted as population annotation accuracy or physical ground truth. The original audio/OOD restrictions, PHM target uncertainty and broader generalization limits remain.\n\nNumerical evidence remains bounded and traceable; human review, annotation adjudication and calibrated wording are the remaining validity work. No further architecture search is authorized by this audit.\n')
